# Source: Ventrax AV4 report. Acceptance specification; execution is verified separately.
Feature: Telemetry ingestion and device validation

  Scenario: Store an authorized telemetry reading
    Given an active device with a valid association
    And a telemetry message with a unique eventId and supported schemaVersion
    When the device publishes the message to its authorized MQTT topic
    Then the reading is accepted and persisted in InfluxDB

  Scenario: Reject a duplicate telemetry event
    Given a reading has already been processed using its eventId
    When the same MQTT message is received again
    Then the service does not persist a duplicate reading

  Scenario: Reject a reading from an unauthorized device
    Given a device does not have a valid association
    When the device publishes telemetry
    Then the event is rejected without storing a reading
